IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `crm-time`

-- Crimes Act 1914 (Commonwealth) -- sections 4K, 4L, 4M and 4N: continuing
-- and multiple offences, specified defences, and the liability of children.
--
-- Each rule answers MAYBE BOOLEAN. JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE only where the text
-- says so in its own words ("shall not", "cannot", "only if", "unless", "does
-- not"); NOTHING where the text limits its reach without "only", lists without
-- closing the list, or does not speak. The days, ages and sums are worked out
-- in crm-time.l4.

§ `Crimes Act 1914 (Cth) ss 4K-4N: continuing offences, defences, children`

§§ `Section 4K(1): continuing obligations`

-- src:4446 | (1) Where, under a law of the Commonwealth, an act or thing is required to be done within a particular period or before a particular time, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the obligation to do that act or thing continues, notwithstanding that the period has expired or the time has passed, until the act or thing is done.
@ref s 4K(1) (src:4446)
GIVEN `under a law of the Commonwealth an act or thing is required to be done within a particular period or before a particular time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period has expired or the time has passed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or thing has been done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4K(1) the obligation to do that act or thing continues` IS
    IF NOT `under a law of the Commonwealth an act or thing is required to be done within a particular period or before a particular time`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `a contrary intention appears`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `the act or thing has been done`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE IF `the period has expired or the time has passed` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 4K(2): an offence for each day`

-- src:4447 | (2) Where a refusal or failure to comply with a requirement referred to in subsection (1) is an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, a person commits an offence in respect of each day during which the person refuses or fails to comply with that requirement, including the day of a conviction for any such offence or any later day.
@ref s 4K(2) (src:4447)
GIVEN `the requirement is one referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a refusal or failure to comply with the requirement is an offence against a law of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person refuses or fails to comply with the requirement during the day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4K(2) the person commits an offence in respect of the day` IS
    IF NOT (`the requirement is one referred to in subsection (1)` AND `a refusal or failure to comply with the requirement is an offence against a law of the Commonwealth`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the person refuses or fails to comply with the requirement during the day` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 4K(3) and (4): joinder and one penalty`

-- src:4448 | (3) Charges against the same person for any number of offences against the same provision of a law of the Commonwealth may be joined in the same information, complaint or summons if those charges are founded on the same facts, or form, or are part of, a series of offences of the same or a similar character.
@ref s 4K(3) (src:4448)
GIVEN `the charges are against the same person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offences are against the same provision of a law of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charges are founded on the same facts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charges form, or are part of, a series of offences of the same or a similar character` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4K(3) the charges may be joined in the same information, complaint or summons` IS
    IF NOT (`the charges are against the same person` AND `the offences are against the same provision of a law of the Commonwealth`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the charges are founded on the same facts` OR `the charges form, or are part of, a series of offences of the same or a similar character`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4449 | (4) If a person is convicted of 2 or more offences referred to in subsection (3), the court may impose one penalty in respect of both or all of those offences, but that penalty shall not exceed the sum of the maximum penalties that could be imposed if a separate penalty were imposed in respect of each offence.
@ref s 4K(4) (src:4449)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of 2 or more offences referred to in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4K(4) the court may impose one penalty in respect of both or all of those offences` IS
    IF `the person is convicted of 2 or more offences referred to in subsection (3)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- "that penalty shall not exceed the sum of the maximum penalties that could
-- be imposed if a separate penalty were imposed in respect of each offence".
-- src:4449 | (4) If a person is convicted of 2 or more offences referred to in subsection (3), the court may impose one penalty in respect of both or all of those offences, but that penalty shall not exceed the sum of the maximum penalties that could be imposed if a separate penalty were imposed in respect of each offence.
@ref s 4K(4) (src:4449)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of 2 or more offences referred to in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum penalties of the separate offences` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4K(4) the most the one penalty may be` IS
    IF `the person is convicted of 2 or more offences referred to in subsection (3)`
    THEN `the sum of the maximum penalties of 2 or more offences` `the maximum penalties of the separate offences`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 4L: specified defences`

-- src:4451 | Where a provision of a law of the Commonwealth provides a defence to a particular offence, the provision does not, unless the contrary intention appears, prevent the use of any defence that is otherwise available.
@ref s 4L (src:4451)
GIVEN `a provision of a law of the Commonwealth provides a defence to a particular offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4L the provision does not prevent the use of any defence that is otherwise available` IS
    IF NOT `a provision of a law of the Commonwealth provides a defence to a particular offence`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Sections 4M and 4N: children`

-- src:4453 | A child under 10 years old cannot be liable for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth.
@ref s 4M (src:4453)
GIVEN `the age of the child in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4M a child can be liable for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth` IS
    IF `the age of the child in years` LESS THAN `s 4M the age below which a child cannot be liable, in years`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4455 | (1) A child aged 10 years or more but under 14 years old can only be liable for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth if the child knows that his or her conduct is wrong.
@ref s 4N(1) (src:4455)
GIVEN `the age of the child in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the child knows that his or her conduct is wrong` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4N(1) a child can be liable for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth` IS
    IF     `the age of the child in years` AT LEAST `s 4N(1) the age from which a child can be liable, in years`
       AND `the age of the child in years` LESS THAN `s 4N(1) the age below which a child can only be liable if the child knows the conduct is wrong, in years`
    THEN (IF `the child knows that his or her conduct is wrong` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Sections 4M and 4N(1) together: a child under 10 cannot be liable, and a
-- child of 10 or more but under 14 can be liable only if the child knows. A
-- child who knows, or is 14 or more, is not made liable by these sections.
-- src:4453 | A child under 10 years old cannot be liable for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth.
-- src:4454 | 4N Children over 10 but under 14
-- src:4455 | (1) A child aged 10 years or more but under 14 years old can only be liable for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth if the child knows that his or her conduct is wrong.
@ref ss 4M, 4N(1) (src:4453-4455)
GIVEN `the age of the child in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the child knows that his or her conduct is wrong` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 4M and 4N(1) a child can be liable for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth` IS
    CONSIDER `s 4M a child can be liable for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth` `the age of the child in years`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE `s 4N(1) a child can be liable for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth` `the age of the child in years` `the child knows that his or her conduct is wrong`

DECLARE PartyToProceedings IS ONE OF
    Prosecution
    Defence

-- src:4456 | (2) The question whether a child knows that his or her conduct is wrong is one of fact. The burden of proving this is on the prosecution.
@ref s 4N(2) (src:4456)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4N(2) the question whether a child knows that his or her conduct is wrong is one of fact` MEANS TRUE

-- src:4456 | (2) The question whether a child knows that his or her conduct is wrong is one of fact. The burden of proving this is on the prosecution.
@ref s 4N(2) (src:4456)
GIVETH A PartyToProceedings
`s 4N(2) the party on whom the burden of proving that the child knows rests` MEANS Prosecution
